<title>GREECE: TABLE - Greek/Bund gap shrinks to 381 bps,288 vs BTP.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Greek/Bund gap shrinks to 381 bps,288 vs BTP.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The spread of Greece's 10-year bond over bunds edged down to 381 basis points today from 382 on Monday.</p>
<p>The Greek/BTP gap also decreased to 288 basis points from 297 on Monday.</p>
<p>		 CPN     MATURITY  YIELDS    SPREADS    PREVIOUS</p>
<p>								    SPREADS</p>
<p>   GREECE    8.80%   25JUN07    9.42%</p>
<p>   GERMANY   6.0%    04JUL07    5.61%	381	382 bps</p>
<p>   FRANCE    5.5%    25APR07    5.47%	395	402 bps</p>
<p>   ITALY     6.75%   01FEB07    6.54%	288	297 bps</p>
<p>   PORTUGAL  6.63%   23FEB07    6.28%	314	305 bps</p>
<p>   SPAIN     7.35%   31MAR07    6.25%	317	313 bps</p>
<p>   UK	  7.25%   07DEC07    7.21%	221	223 bps</p>
<p>   US	  6.63%   15MAY07    6.37%	305	306 bps</p>
<p>All yields are annualised and based on bid prices at 0936 GMT. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
